--- a/TODO.md
+++ b/TODO.md
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ The schema items below change generated columns of `txn`. Because `CREATE TABLE
 - `schema.sql:27` — the index name `txn_date` says neither which date it covers nor that it is per account. `txn_account_booking_date` would. An existing db keeps the old index, so drop it as part of the migration.
 - `pyproject.toml:19` and `seb.py` `Store.__init__` — the schema file's name and its place next to the module are spelled in both files. Renaming either breaks only an installed `seb`. The wheel also installs a bare `schema.sql` at the top level of site-packages. Options: move the code into a `dengi/` package and load the schema with `importlib.resources`, or embed the schema in `seb.py` as a string. Either one changes how the program is laid out and run.
 - `.gitignore:3-5` and `seb.py` `DB`, `Session.PATH`, `Config.from_env` (`private.pem`) — every runtime file sits in the current directory, and `.gitignore` has to repeat each name. A new state file can be committed by accident, and these files hold bank data, a consent and a private key. Keep the runtime state in one directory, for example the XDG state directory, and ignore that directory.
-- `seb.py` `Session.parse` — a `valid_until` without a timezone parses, and the comparison with `datetime.now(UTC)` in `Session.load` then raises a TypeError instead of a BankError. Reject a naive `valid_until` in `Session.parse`.
+- `seb.py` `Session.parse` — a `valid_until` without a timezone parses, and the comparison with `datetime.now(UTC)` in `Session.expired` then raises a TypeError instead of a BankError. Reject a naive `valid_until` in `Session.parse`.
 - `seb.py` `user_ip` and `EnableBanking.call` — a network failure, a failed ipify call, or a body that is not JSON raises a `requests` exception or a `ValueError`. Neither is a BankError, so the run ends in a traceback. Decide whether these should become BankError.
 - `seb.py` `Transaction.booked` and `Account.parse` — `entry_reference`, and an account's `uid` and `iban`, are typed `str` but never checked. A null `uid` ends up in the transactions URL and in `txn.iban`. A null or numeric value gets through and fails later, in `Store.upsert_counting_new`, with an sqlite IntegrityError or a non-text key. Check their types where they are parsed.
 - `seb.py` `Transaction.parse` and `Store.last_booking_date` — `booking_date` is first parsed when a later run resumes. A malformed value then raises ValueError on every run after it. Parse the date when the transaction is read, or add a `CHECK (date(booking_date) IS booking_date)` to the schema together with the migration.
